  "summary": "The Independent Institute opinion piece surveys cases of police officers misusing Flock and other ALPR systems to stalk ex-partners and women, including charged IMPD officers, a Kentucky officer who ran 2,000+ searches, and an Orange City, Florida officer. The author argues internal policies are insufficient and calls for real-time audits, judicial authorization for historic location tracking, and notice to those searched.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "at least 50 law enforcement officers around the country had been accused or charged with misusing Flock and other automated license plate reader (ALPR) systems",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "used the Flock system \"more than 950 times in a six-month period\" to track his ex-wife's movements",
      "paragraph_idx": 3
    },
    {
      "quote": "462 agencies and institutions have \"terminated, suspended, or declined to renew\" their contracts",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "audits that flag misuse in real time, judicial authorization before law enforcement can conduct historic location tracking, and notice to individuals whose data is searched outside an active investigation",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    }
  ],
